at handles steering, acceleration, and braking.\n\nTarget Speed – Sets the autopilot cruising speed from 150 to 280 mph.\n\nPass Distance – Adjusts the spacing used when overtaking vehicles from 8 to 22 studs.\n\nMinimum Gap – Sets the minimum distance maintained from vehicles ahead from 5 to 18 studs.\n\nCaution Level – Adjusts the autopilot's driving aggression from 0% to 100%.\n\nSeek Overtakes – Allows the autopilot to actively look for opportunities to pass other vehicles.\n\nAvoid Crashes – Helps avoid collisions with vehicles and obstacles.\n\nKeep Level – Stabilizes the vehicle to keep it level with the road during high-speed driving.\n\nRoute recording and pathing\n\nRecord Route – Records a custom driving line or lap while you drive manually.\n\nFollow Route – Automatically follows a previously recorded driving route.\n\nClear Route – Deletes the currently recorded route.\n\nRoute Status – Displays whether a route is recording, idle, or currently being followed.\n\nGarage and customization\n\nCar Spawner – Automatically identifies and spawns the best owned vehicle based on top speed, horsepower, and price.\n\nCar Skin Changer – Replaces the current vehicle model with another available car model.\n\nCar List Refresh – Refreshes the vehicle list with currently available cars.\n\nRestore Own Car – Restores the original vehicle model after using a different skin.\n\nLive status monitoring\n\nCurrent Speed – Displays your current speed in mph.\n\nOvertakes – Tracks the number of successful overtakes during the session.\n\nPer Minute – Displays the average overtake rate.\n\nCombo Left – Shows the remaining time on the current overtake combo.\n\nAutopilot State – Displays the current autopilot state, such as Engaging, Scanning, Routing, or Error.\n\nCar Name – Displays the name of the current vehicle.\n\nInterface and session\n\nMenu Keybind – Changes the key used to toggle the SnowyHub interface, defaulting to RightShift.\n\nWatermark – Displays a compact on-scr